Direct3D 12 renderer: the OpenGL renderer, compiled a second time on D3D12.

renderer = "d3d12" (settings.toml / game.toml / --renderer d3d12; value 3).

Not a second renderer. gpu_gl_renderer.c and gpu_gl_postfx.c are compiled
twice: once as always, and once (gpu_gl_renderer_d3d12.c,
gpu_gl_postfx_d3d12.c) with PSX_GL_ON_D3D12, where gpu_gl12.h redirects every
GL call the renderer makes - the GL 1.1 entry points, the modern ones it
fetches through SDL_GL_GetProcAddress, and SDL_GL_CreateContext / SwapWindow
/ GetDrawableSize / SetSwapInterval - to a GL-subset layer on Direct3D 12
(gpu_gl12.cpp). VRAM coherency, batching, mask/stencil, semi-transparency
(dual-source blending), texture windows, the native-wide compositor, frame
interpolation, hold-last, 24-bit FMV, bezels, the OSD, post-processing, the
heartbeat cost counters and frame_perf are the same code on both APIs, and
stay the same as the GL side changes: parity by construction.

gpu_gl12.cpp keeps the renderer's GL assumptions true:
  - Row r of a GL framebuffer is row r of the D3D12 resource; vertex shaders
    negate clip-space y, so viewports, scissors, blits, texel fetches,
    gl_FragCoord and readbacks use the same numbers on both APIs.
  - Framebuffer 0 is an offscreen texture at window size in that convention;
    SwapWindow draws it into the flip-discard swap chain flipped (tearing
    allowed with vsync off, at most two frames queued). Reading "the default
    framebuffer" (hold-last) is then an ordinary copy.
  - GLSL is not compiled: each GLSL source is matched by FNV-1a hash of its
    exact text to a hand-written HLSL translation (gl12_hlsl/*.hlsl, table
    generated into gpu_gl12_shaders.h by gl12_hlsl/gen_gl12_shaders.py). An
    unknown source fails to compile, so a GLSL edit without its HLSL twin
    stops D3D12 from starting instead of drawing wrong. HLSL is compiled at
    startup by d3dcompiler_47.dll (part of Windows) and cached as DXBC in
    <exe>/shadercache.
  - Pipeline states are built on demand from the GL state at draw time and
    cached; resource states are tracked per texture; upload memory, shader-
    visible descriptors and deleted resources are recycled by fence; queries
    are timestamp pairs; glFenceSync / pixel-pack buffers back the
    asynchronous rewind download. Wide GL lines are a geometry shader that
    widens along the minor axis as GL does.
  - PSX_D3D12_DEBUG=1 enables the debug layer and prints its messages;
    PSX_GL12_DUMP=<prefix> writes every presented frame as a PPM.

gpu_gl_names.h gives each compilation's public functions its own prefix
(glimpl_ / d3d12impl_); gpu_hw_dispatch.c (generated from the exported
symbols) provides the public gl_renderer_* / gl_backend_get names and routes
each call to the API gl_renderer_select_d3d12() chose. The debug-control and
diagnostic globals (g_ws_bd_*, g_bdg_*, g_ptrace, g_gl_swap_total) exist once
and are shared, so the heartbeat and debug server work on either API.

main.cpp: "d3d12" resolves to the GL path with g_video_d3d12 set - no
SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL on the window, the D3D12 context, "d3d12" in the latency
ring and log. If D3D12 cannot start (no feature-level 11 device, no
d3dcompiler_47, a failed shader) the window is recreated GL-capable, the
OpenGL copy is set up the way gpu_init and the scale code set up the other,
and the game runs on OpenGL. The bezel and frame-interpolation mod hooks no
longer downgrade a D3D12 choice to OpenGL. Builds without D3D12 (non-Windows)
treat the request as OpenGL.

Verified offline with a harness that drives both compilations through the
same vtable (textured 4/8/15-bit, CLUTs, modulation, all semi-transparency
modes, texture window, mask set/check, fills, copies, lines, draw area and
offset, CPU pokes and readbacks) and captures every present: at 1x, 2x, 3x,
4x and 5x the read-back VRAM is bit-identical to OpenGL and every presented
frame - 4:3, letterbox with bezel, the CPU/FMV path, hold-last, native-wide,
blank - is byte-identical; the async readback equals the synchronous one;
SMAA, FXAA, CAS and texture dedither are byte-identical, bloom and the grade
within 1/255 (float rounding). The debug layer reports nothing.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.
config_loader.* are compiled into the runtime, not part of the codegen tag.

